    "result_text": "Full suite is green (12 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner response, mirroring the existing `displayName` convention in this codebase.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only string), right after `displayName`. This regenerates the `OwnerDto` with an `initials` field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes `initials` as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot:\n   ```java\n   Character.toUpperCase(firstName.charAt(0)) + \".\" + Character.toUpperCase(lastName.charAt(0)) + \".\"\n   ```\n   For `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`.\n\nSince `GET /api/owners/{id}` already responds via `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)`, no OfficeFloor function or YAML wiring needed to change \u2014 the new field flows through automatically.\n\n`Cp06Tests` passes and all 12 acceptance tests remain green.",
